@baseUrl = http://localhost:5280
@mailboxAddress = tobys@6w020f.onmicrosoft.com
@mailboxId = 50a1bff5-7bc4-4da0-824e-07ac4014571f
@messageId = REPLACE-WITH-GRAPH-MESSAGE-ID
@subscriptionId = REPLACE-WITH-GRAPH-SUBSCRIPTION-ID

###
# ─── IGraphMailClient ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every request here calls live Microsoft Graph. Supply credentials first (see README.md).
###

### IGraphMailClient.ResolveMailboxIdAsync
### Expect 200 with { "mailboxId": "<guid-like id>" }, or { "mailboxId": null } if the user does
### not exist. Copy the returned id into @mailboxId above — every request below needs it.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/mailboxes/{{mailboxAddress}}/id

###

### IGraphMailClient.GetWellKnownFolderIdsAsync
### Expect 200 with inboxFolderId and sentItemsFolderId populated. If Graph 404s one folder, that
### id comes back null while the other still resolves.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/mailboxes/{{mailboxId}}/folders

###

### IGraphMailClient.GetMessageAsync (full, 3-arg)
### Expect 200 with the mapped message: mailboxId stamped, body/uniqueBody trimmed, and inReplyTo
### plus references recovered from the MAPI extended properties (references most-recent-first).
### Returns 200 with a null body if the message id does not exist.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/mailboxes/{{mailboxId}}/messages/{{messageId}}

###

### IGraphMailClient.GetMessageAsync<T> (generic, with selectFields)
### Deserializes into JsonNode, so any field set works (T is constrained to reference types so a
### missing message can come back as null). Expect 200 echoing exactly the fields requested and
### nothing else, or 200 with a null body if the message id does not exist. Sending fields= (empty)
### makes the library throw ArgumentException, which the harness surfaces as a 500.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/mailboxes/{{mailboxId}}/messages/{{messageId}}/select?fields=id,subject,receivedDateTime

###

### IGraphMailClient.UpdateMessageCategoriesAsync
### Expect 204 No Content, and the new categories visible on the message in Outlook. The supplied
### array REPLACES the existing categories; a Graph failure surfaces as a 500.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/graph/mailboxes/{{mailboxId}}/messages/{{messageId}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

["AI - LEGAL", "AI - URGENT"]

###

### IGraphMailClient.GetMessagesDeltaAsync
### First call (no deltaLink): expect 200 with messages received since floor, plus a deltaLink to
### persist. Pass that deltaLink back on the next call to get only what changed since. An expired
### token makes the library restart from floor (410 handling) rather than replay all history.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/mailboxes/{{mailboxId}}/delta?floor=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z

###
